00:17:13.665 --> 00:17:15.167
that people should know?

00:17:16.568 --> 00:17:17.403
- Well...

00:17:19.071 --> 00:17:22.541
The fact is that based on
biochemical individuality,

00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:23.909
different shapes of the stomach,

00:17:23.909 --> 00:17:25.477
the pancreas, the liver,

00:17:25.477 --> 00:17:27.546
different vitamin
D excretion rates

00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:28.814
and different ways

00:17:28.814 --> 00:17:31.417
that we all process food
as unique human beings,

00:17:31.417 --> 00:17:32.551
paired with the fact

00:17:32.551 --> 00:17:34.053 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we all have
unique genetics, right?

00:17:34.053 --> 00:17:35.287
Like someone from,

00:17:35.287 --> 00:17:36.822
let's say, Sub-Saharan Africa

00:17:36.822 --> 00:17:40.426 align:start size:97% position:3%
is going to do far better
based on equatorial location

00:17:40.426 --> 00:17:43.262
and sun exposure
to high carb intake

00:17:43.262 --> 00:17:45.097
and lots of fruits

00:17:45.097 --> 00:17:48.400
and a lower amount of
like saturated fats,

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
compared to someone
Northern European descent

00:17:50.402 --> 00:17:52.504 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
who does really
good on like fish,

00:17:52.504 --> 00:17:54.606 line:0%
steak, fermented foods...

00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:55.507 line:0%
High fat milk,

00:17:55.507 --> 00:17:57.509 align:start size:75% position:25% line:0%
stuff like that.
- Mm-hmm.

00:17:57.509 --> 00:18:00.579 align:start position:0%
- The idea is that it's not
gonna be the same for everybody,

00:18:00.579 --> 00:18:02.281
but we live in an era in which

00:18:02.281 --> 00:18:05.184
the same type of self
quantification tests

00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:07.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
that would have cost like
tens of thousands of dollars,

00:18:07.386 --> 00:18:08.554
let's say like,

00:18:08.554 --> 00:18:09.922 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Princeton
Longevity Institute,

00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:11.156
or Duke,

00:18:11.156 --> 00:18:13.492
or any of these places
where a lot of execs

00:18:13.492 --> 00:18:15.494
would normally get
tested to really,

00:18:15.494 --> 00:18:17.563 align:start size:84% position:16%
really dial in
something like diet

00:18:17.563 --> 00:18:19.431
or nutrition or supplementation,

00:18:19.431 --> 00:18:20.666
those are available to us

00:18:20.666 --> 00:18:21.967
in the comfort of
our own home now

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:24.336
for a fraction of the cost,

00:18:24.336 --> 00:18:26.004
so people can test their blood,

00:18:26.004 --> 00:18:27.606
they can test their genetics,

00:18:27.606 --> 00:18:29.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
they can test their
stool for like

00:18:29.341 --> 00:18:30.609
what the gut is asking for,

00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:34.246
and by testing your body,

00:18:34.246 --> 00:18:36.148
by looking at your genetics,

00:18:36.148 --> 00:18:37.549
and by paying attention

00:18:37.549 --> 00:18:40.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
to your own unique
biochemical individuality,

00:18:40.419 --> 00:18:42.821
you should be able to
tweak your diet to you,

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:44.189
and what I mean by that is like

00:18:44.189 --> 00:18:46.658
the same ketogenic diet

00:18:46.658 --> 00:18:48.927 align:start size:84% position:16%
that your neighbor
used to lose 20 pounds

00:18:48.927 --> 00:18:50.796
might be super crappy for you

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:52.030
and cause inflammation

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:55.234
and weight gain in you
because you have a liver

00:18:55.234 --> 00:18:57.402 align:start size:84% position:16%
and gallbladder that
isn't processing

00:18:57.402 --> 00:18:59.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
that high intake of
saturated fats very well,

00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:00.906
or you have,

00:19:00.906 --> 00:19:03.142
let's say, like an APOE e4 gene,

00:19:03.142 --> 00:19:04.409
which would dictate

00:19:04.409 --> 00:19:06.311
that high intake of
fats predisposes you

00:19:06.311 --> 00:19:08.480
to Alzheimer's or dementia,

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:11.150
or you have poor
enzyme production

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.618
that dictates that
you can't burn fats

00:19:12.618 --> 00:19:14.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
that well because you
don't have enough lipase.

00:19:14.453 --> 00:19:17.456 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that's just one
example of the fact

00:19:17.456 --> 00:19:19.391
that there is no one diet

00:19:19.391 --> 00:19:20.859
that works well for everyone.

00:19:20.859 --> 00:19:22.561
And that being said,

00:19:22.561 --> 00:19:23.929 align:start size:81% position:19%
a couple of things
to think about,

00:19:23.929 --> 00:19:25.197
first of all,

00:19:25.197 --> 00:19:28.133 align:start position:0%
when you look at
epidemiological data for a wide,

00:19:28.133 --> 00:19:30.302
wide variety of the
world's populations,

00:19:30.302 --> 00:19:33.071 align:start size:88% position:13%
probably because humans
likely originated

00:19:33.071 --> 00:19:34.773
somewhere in the
Fertile Crescent,

00:19:34.773 --> 00:19:37.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
something along the lines
of like a low carbish

00:19:37.609 --> 00:19:40.679 align:start size:88% position:13%
Mediterranean diet tends
to work really well

00:19:40.679 --> 00:19:42.181
for a lot of people...

00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.917
Not like an Olive Garden
unlimited breadsticks diet,

00:19:44.917 --> 00:19:47.486 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I mean like a diet
very rich in herbs

00:19:47.486 --> 00:19:51.690 align:start size:88% position:13%
and spices and a wide
variety of plant matter,

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.592
some amounts of fish and eggs,

00:19:53.592 --> 00:19:55.460
red meat, but in moderation,

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:57.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
lots of healthy
omega-3 fatty acids,

00:19:57.429 --> 00:19:58.597
not only from those fish,

00:19:58.597 --> 00:20:00.165 align:start size:84% position:16%
but things like extra
virgin olive oil

00:20:00.165 --> 00:20:02.167
and avocados and avocado oil

00:20:02.167 --> 00:20:03.368
and seeds and nuts,

00:20:03.368 --> 00:20:05.571
like that low carb
Mediterranean profile

00:20:05.571 --> 00:20:07.072
tends to be something

00:20:07.072 --> 00:20:08.607
that seems to agree
with a lot of people.

00:20:08.607 --> 00:20:11.643
And then when you look
at these blue zones,

00:20:11.643 --> 00:20:13.478 align:start size:88% position:13%
these longevity hotspots
around the world

00:20:13.478 --> 00:20:15.414
like Nicoya and Ikaria

00:20:15.414 --> 00:20:18.750
and Sardinia and Loma Linda,

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.720
even though the
diets widely vary

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.323
in terms of low
carb, high fat...

00:20:24.323 --> 00:20:25.824
High carb, low fat,

00:20:25.824 --> 00:20:27.025
different plants and herbs

00:20:27.025 --> 00:20:28.560 align:start size:84% position:16%
and spices being used
in those regions,

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:31.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
different forms of
alcohol intake, et cetera,

00:20:31.363 --> 00:20:33.699
what we do see in terms of
prevailing characteristics

00:20:33.699 --> 00:20:35.100
in all those regions is,

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.270 align:start position:0%
A, there's always some
semblance of fasting worked in,

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:41.173
a lot of times it's based
on religious concepts...

00:20:41.173 --> 00:20:42.908
Like the Mediterranean diet,

00:20:42.908 --> 00:20:45.611
that's very popular among like
Eastern Orthodox Christians,

00:20:45.611 --> 00:20:48.247
and then there's a ton of
special fasts in that diet,

00:20:48.247 --> 00:20:50.082 align:start size:84% position:16%
certain days where you
don't eat red meat,

00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:51.383
certain periods of time

00:20:51.383 --> 00:20:53.785
where you're avoiding a
high intake of proteins,

00:20:53.785 --> 00:20:55.053
certain periods of time

00:20:55.053 --> 00:20:56.555 align:start size:84% position:16%
where you're just
straight up fasting,

00:20:56.555 --> 00:20:58.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
we see fasting as one
predominant characteristic

00:20:58.323 --> 00:21:00.726
of every single healthy diet
on the face of the planet,

00:21:00.726 --> 00:21:02.261
some type of fasting

00:21:02.261 --> 00:21:04.096
and some type of
time during the day

00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:05.597
or the week

00:21:05.597 --> 00:21:07.532 align:start size:97% position:3%
or the month where you're
not eating a lot of protein,

00:21:07.532 --> 00:21:09.301
'cause protein in high amounts

00:21:09.301 --> 00:21:10.602
can tend to have a little bit

00:21:10.602 --> 00:21:12.204
of an accelerated aging effect.

00:21:13.672 --> 00:21:17.175
We also see the concept of
eating with people, right?

00:21:17.175 --> 00:21:18.910
Not only saying grace

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:20.145
or having a moment of silence

00:21:20.145 --> 00:21:21.947 align:start size:81% position:19%
or having a moment
of appreciation

00:21:21.947 --> 00:21:23.915
or sacredness around a meal,

00:21:23.915 --> 00:21:25.884
but also not stuffing your face

00:21:25.884 --> 00:21:27.352
with a super food smoothie

00:21:27.352 --> 00:21:30.322
while you're going 65 miles
an hour down the highway

00:21:30.322 --> 00:21:31.823
on your way to work,

00:21:31.823 --> 00:21:33.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead, and I'm highly
kind of doing this myself,

00:21:33.225 --> 00:21:34.660
if I'm gonna eat,

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:37.029 align:start size:97% position:3%
I always eat in what's called
a parasympathetic state,

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:38.263
I sit down,

00:21:38.263 --> 00:21:39.631
I do a little...

00:21:39.631 --> 00:21:40.966
Just a few centering breaths,

00:21:40.966 --> 00:21:42.401
like in through the nose,

00:21:42.401 --> 00:21:43.235
out through the mouth,

00:21:43.235 --> 00:21:44.202
I say grace,

00:21:44.202 --> 00:21:47.172
I chew each bite 25 to 40 times,

00:21:47.172 --> 00:21:48.740
I try to eat with people

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
so I'm not distracted
by my computer,

00:21:50.475 --> 00:21:51.677
by my phone,

00:21:51.677 --> 00:21:53.245 align:start size:84% position:16%
but instead, I'm
visiting with people,

00:21:53.245 --> 00:21:55.180
and we see that as another
predominant characteristic

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.381
of a healthy diet,

00:21:56.381 --> 00:21:57.916 align:start size:84% position:16%
like eating in a
very low stress state

00:21:57.916 --> 00:21:59.184
and eating with people.

00:21:59.184 --> 00:22:01.853
And then you also see

00:22:01.853 --> 00:22:04.623 align:start size:84% position:16%
a wide intake of a
huge variety of plants

00:22:04.623 --> 00:22:05.924
and herbs and spices,

00:22:05.924 --> 00:22:06.858
and I realized

00:22:06.858 --> 00:22:08.827
that diets like the paleo diet

00:22:08.827 --> 00:22:10.228
or the carnivore diet,

00:22:10.228 --> 00:22:12.731 align:start position:0%
or a lot of these highly
restrictive diets have popped up

00:22:12.731 --> 00:22:14.800 align:start size:88% position:13%
and become very
popular over the years,

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:16.435
and a big premise of those diets

00:22:16.435 --> 00:22:17.969
is that they eliminate

00:22:17.969 --> 00:22:20.939 align:start size:88% position:13%
a lot of built-in plant
defense mechanisms,

00:22:20.939 --> 00:22:22.174
like plants can't move,

00:22:22.174 --> 00:22:24.409
and so because they
don't have hooves

00:22:24.409 --> 00:22:25.344
and teeth and claws,

00:22:25.344 --> 00:22:27.179
they develop things like gluten

00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:28.447
and lectins and other things

00:22:28.447 --> 00:22:30.615
that would cause a mammal's gut

00:22:30.615 --> 00:22:32.217
to be a little bit disturbed,

00:22:32.217 --> 00:22:34.820
cause that mammal to
poop out the seeds

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:36.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
of that plant elsewhere
so that plant can flourish

00:22:36.855 --> 00:22:39.424
or cause that mammal not
to come back to that plant

00:22:39.424 --> 00:22:41.360 align:start size:84% position:16%
to eat it again cause
it kind of hurt.

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:43.562
And so if you have
a compromised gut,

00:22:43.562 --> 00:22:45.097
or if you have the inability

00:22:45.097 --> 00:22:46.865
to be able to do like our
ancestors would have done

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:48.700
and soak and sprout and ferment

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:51.002
and properly prepare a
lot of your plant matter,

00:22:51.002 --> 00:22:52.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
then yeah, doing
something like a paleo

00:22:52.871 --> 00:22:55.574 align:start size:81% position:19%
or a carnivore
diet has efficacy.

00:22:56.808 --> 00:22:58.977
However, in people
with healthy guts

00:22:58.977 --> 00:23:00.412 align:start size:84% position:16%
who don't have a lot
of health issues,

00:23:00.412 --> 00:23:01.913
like a wide variety of plants

00:23:01.913 --> 00:23:05.417
and herbs and spices really
seems to induce longevity

00:23:05.417 --> 00:23:06.718 align:start size:81% position:19%
and be a healthier
form of a diet,

00:23:06.718 --> 00:23:07.986
and that's another thing

00:23:07.986 --> 00:23:08.920
we see in a lot of
these blue zones,

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:09.788
they're not highly restricted,

00:23:09.788 --> 00:23:11.857
they eat a huge variety,

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:13.291
like a hundred plus
different plants

00:23:13.291 --> 00:23:14.126
and herbs and spices,

00:23:14.126 --> 00:23:15.127
whereas here in America,

00:23:15.127 --> 00:23:16.361
we often...

00:23:16.361 --> 00:23:17.696
I think we're somewhere
around like 15 to 20.

00:23:17.696 --> 00:23:18.630
- Right.
- And so...

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:19.698
- And so would you say the paleo

00:23:19.698 --> 00:23:20.599
and carnivore,

00:23:20.599 --> 00:23:21.533
that kind of stuff,

00:23:21.533 --> 00:23:22.968
like it's sort of short term

00:23:22.968 --> 00:23:25.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
to help fix the gut
inflammation kind of stuff

00:23:25.103 --> 00:23:27.606
but not necessarily long-term?

00:23:27.606 --> 00:23:29.040 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, let's say
you have a leaky gut,

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.410
you have inflammation issues,

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:32.844
you need to kind of
give your gut a break

00:23:32.844 --> 00:23:34.312
or you need to not
have a lot of gluten,

00:23:34.312 --> 00:23:35.147
a lot of lectins,

00:23:35.147 --> 00:23:36.114
a lot of dairy...

00:23:36.114 --> 00:23:37.382
Follow a carnivore diet

00:23:37.382 --> 00:23:39.785
or a paleo diet for
like 12 to 16 weeks

00:23:39.785 --> 00:23:40.986
to allow your gut to heal

00:23:40.986 --> 00:23:42.354
and re-stabilize,

00:23:42.354 --> 00:23:45.424 align:start size:97% position:3%
but then begin to
reincorporate things like...

00:23:45.424 --> 00:23:47.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
Whatever, kale and
cucumbers and tomatoes

00:23:47.626 --> 00:23:49.428
and all those foods

00:23:49.428 --> 00:23:51.029 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you might've
been missing out on.

00:23:51.029 --> 00:23:54.099
And then probably
the final big thing

00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:56.601
that we see in a lot of
these healthy locations

00:23:56.601 --> 00:23:58.737
is not the absence
of sugar, right?

00:23:58.737 --> 00:23:59.905
We actually see a
lot of these play,

00:23:59.905 --> 00:24:00.939
like they like their chocolates,

00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:02.841 align:start size:88% position:13%
they like their sweets.
- Mm-hmm.

00:24:02.841 --> 00:24:03.809
- They like their candies,

00:24:03.809 --> 00:24:06.111
you look at the analysis of...

00:24:06.111 --> 00:24:07.479
Centenarians are people...

00:24:07.479 --> 00:24:08.713
In many cases,

00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:09.948 align:start size:81% position:19%
who have lived 115
plus years old,

00:24:09.948 --> 00:24:11.450
I was reading a
fantastic article

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:14.753 align:start size:97% position:3%
the other day about like 20
different 115 year old people,

00:24:14.753 --> 00:24:16.254
and a lot of them...

00:24:16.254 --> 00:24:17.889
They comment, "Oh, I love to
have my chocolate every day."

00:24:17.889 --> 00:24:20.058
"I love my sweets."

00:24:20.058 --> 00:24:21.560
And there's even some of them

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:23.595
that would like smoke a
cigarette a day and heal,

00:24:23.595 --> 00:24:24.796
but the one thing

00:24:24.796 --> 00:24:27.199 align:start size:81% position:19%
that you'll notice
in these folks

00:24:27.199 --> 00:24:29.468 align:start size:88% position:13%
and also in a lot of
these longevity hotspots

00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:32.504
is almost complete absence of
vegetable oil intake, right?

00:24:32.504 --> 00:24:36.141
Canola oil, safflower
oil, sunflower oil,

00:24:36.141 --> 00:24:38.109
a lot of these vegetable oils

00:24:38.109 --> 00:24:41.313 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we tend to see
especially in processed

00:24:41.313 --> 00:24:42.781
and packaged foods

00:24:42.781 --> 00:24:44.683
or used in restaurants to cook,

00:24:44.683 --> 00:24:45.784
and the reason for that

00:24:45.784 --> 00:24:48.253
is because vegetable oils,

00:24:48.253 --> 00:24:49.187
based on the fact

00:24:49.187 --> 00:24:50.388
that they're comprised of fats,

00:24:50.388 --> 00:24:52.757
are what your body
uses to create things

00:24:52.757 --> 00:24:55.994 align:start size:88% position:13%
like cell membranes,
cholesterol,
mitochondrial membranes,

00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:58.663 align:start size:88% position:13%
your body uses these
oils as building blocks,

00:24:58.663 --> 00:25:01.900 align:start size:88% position:13%
and if they are unstable
oils, rancid oils,

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.168
oils that have been exposed

00:25:03.168 --> 00:25:05.036
to high amounts of
heat or pressure,

00:25:05.036 --> 00:25:07.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
what happens is
those vegetable oils

00:25:07.706 --> 00:25:08.673
really truly become

00:25:08.673 --> 00:25:10.876
a case of you are what you eat,

00:25:10.876 --> 00:25:12.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they create
rampant inflammation,

00:25:12.944 --> 00:25:15.981 align:start size:84% position:16%
weak cell membranes,
poor metabolism,

00:25:15.981 --> 00:25:17.182
and so...

00:25:17.182 --> 00:25:18.617
Whereas sugar isn't
as big of a deal

00:25:18.617 --> 00:25:19.985
as most people think,

00:25:19.985 --> 00:25:20.952
vegetable oils...

00:25:20.952 --> 00:25:21.786
I tell people,

00:25:21.786 --> 00:25:23.154
"You wanna be healthy?"

00:25:23.154 --> 00:25:24.689 align:start position:0%
"Ruthlessly eliminate
vegetable oils from your diet."

00:25:24.689 --> 00:25:26.224
And sometimes, that means...

00:25:26.224 --> 00:25:28.460
Like me, if I go
to a restaurant,

00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:29.694
I literally ask them,

00:25:29.694 --> 00:25:31.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
like I'm that asshole
who says like,

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:33.765
"What'd you cook the
Brussels sprouts in?"

00:25:33.765 --> 00:25:35.901
Or, "Can I have my salad

00:25:35.901 --> 00:25:37.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
but bring the
dressing on the side?"

00:25:37.969 --> 00:25:39.404
And then like...

